{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\"\n       xmlns:event=\"https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event\"\n       version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"order\">\n  <state id=\"order\">\n    <onentry>\n      <send event=\"order.placed\" target=\"#_parent\"\n            event:schema='{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"quantity\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"minimum\":1}},\"required\":[\"quantity\"]}'>\n        <content>{\"quantity\": 0}</content>\n      </send>\n    </onentry>\n    <transition target=\"done\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"done\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/event009-literal-payload.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/event009-literal-payload.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":43,"endLine":8,"startColumn":9,"startLine":8}}}],"message":{"markdown":"the literal data of `<send>` does not satisfy its own `event:schema`\n\n**Note:** the `<content>` is literal JSON, so the event data it creates is known before the document runs, and the element's literal `event:schema` describes that data\n\n**Help:** change the `<content>` to data the schema admits, or correct the schema\n\n**Spec:** JSON Schema 2020-12 Validation","text":"the literal data of `<send>` does not satisfy its own `event:schema`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":442,"start":408},"category":"semantic"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"the schema it must satisfy"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/event009-literal-payload.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":126,"endLine":7,"startColumn":13,"startLine":7}}}],"ruleId":"EVENT009"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"in an ECMAScript document, literal JSON `<content>` (no `expr`, text only) is the event data the element creates, known before the document runs, and the element's literal `event:schema` (inline, or a file whose bytes were supplied) describes that data; data the schema rejects breaks the element's own contract. `event:schemaexpr` and schemas that do not resolve are skipped"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: change the `<content>` to data the schema admits, or correct the schema.\n\nSpecification: JSON Schema 2020-12 Validation\n\nRun `scx --explain EVENT009` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/json-schema-validation","id":"EVENT009","name":"EVENT009","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"the literal data of a `<send>` or `<donedata>` does not satisfy its own `event:schema`"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}